course: dictionary
lesson: 2511
title: Decently
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Decently is an adverb, so it tells us how someone does something. It has three main meanings: in a polite, fair and right way; fairly well or well enough; and wearing enough clothes so you are not showing too much. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «Treat people decently» means treat them fairly and kindly. «A job that pays decently» means it pays well enough to live on. «Decently dressed» means wearing proper clothes that cover you. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
explain: In our example, «felt that his skin was now as tight as was decently safe», decently means reasonably, within a sensible limit. The animal has eaten so much that he is as full as is sensible, which is why the sentence is funny. Decent is an adjective, but decently is the adverb form.
fact: Decently is an adverb: it tells us how something is done.
fact: «Decently» means in a polite, fair and respectable way.
fact: «Decently» can mean well enough or fairly well, as in «decently paid».
fact: «Decently» can mean wearing enough clothes, not showing too much.
fact: A quick check is to swap in fairly or reasonably and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Sam's job pays decently, so he can afford a flat.» What does decently mean here? | *Well enough to live on | Not at all | Very loudly | Badly and unfairly
exercise: In «The children were decently dressed for church», what does decently mean? | Sleepily | Wet through from rain | *Wearing enough clothes, not showing too much | Very quickly
exercise: Badger insists that Toad must behave decently. What does decently suggest? | Carelessly and rudely | Very quickly | Loudly, at the top of his voice | *In a polite, fair and right way
test: «He paid the workers decently for their hard work.» What does decently mean? | Only just, barely | *Fairly and well enough | Late and grudgingly | Sadly
test: Which word could replace decently in «The soup was decently hot» without changing the meaning much? | Badly | Quietly | Never | *Fairly
exam: Ruby reads «The men were decently clothed.» What does decently mean? | Angry | Fast | Very wet | *Wearing enough clothes, not showing too much
